{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And you draw out.</b> Like the meaning of ויפק רצון יהוה (Proverbs 8:35), and here your [word] נפשך is in the manner of the [piel] stem." "<b>And the afflicted soul — it satisfies.</b> Affliction is always joined with נפש — it is fasting, and the word תשביע bears witness [to this]." "<b>And shine in darkness.</b> Even in the darkness of night your light shines, and the meaning is: when evil comes upon the world, you escape."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 58, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:07.032366856Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}